.TH WHETSTONE\-TUI 1 "2026\-07\-25" "whetstone\-tui 0.1.4" "Whetstone Manual"
.SH NAME
whetstone\-tui \- a friction\-first Markdown/Quarto editor for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B whetstone\-tui
.RI [ FILE ]
.RI [ SUBCOMMAND ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Whetstone is a friction\-first writing surface for students under honor codes,
shipped as a terminal editor. It keeps the writing yours: pastes are quarantined
and must be rewritten ("claim\-to\-own") or attributed, the optional AI coach can
only ask questions (structured coaching can't ghostwrite by design; free\-text
chat replies are length\-capped and screened, with a small residual risk), and an
append\-only journal lets you export an honest "how this was written" disclosure.
.PP
The product claim is \fIfriction, not proof\fR: Whetstone never claims to verify
who wrote anything. It makes zero outbound network calls unless you configure a
coach endpoint; grammar checking runs locally.
.PP
A bare file path (or none) opens the editor. The subcommands below run
non\-interactively and print JSON, so an agent, script, or CI step can drive the
same core logic.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.BR lint " " \fIFILE\fR " [\fB\-\-strict\fR]"
Run Harper grammar/spell checking; print diagnostics as JSON. With
\fB\-\-strict\fR, exit non-zero when any diagnostics are found (for CI).
.TP
.BR coach " " \fIFILE\fR " \fB\-\-message\fR " \fIMSG\fR " [\fB\-\-journal\fR " \fIFILE\fR "]"
Run one coach turn over the file, screened by the guard (and the judge, if
configured). With \fB\-\-journal\fR, append a metadata-only consult event (and a
\fBJudgeUnavailable\fR event on judge fail-open) so a later \fBdisclosure\fR
render is honest about headless coaching.
.TP
.BR guard " \fB\-\-reply\fR " \fITEXT\fR " [\fB\-\-draft\fR " \fIFILE\fR "]"
Screen an arbitrary reply with the deterministic guard (and the judge, if set).
.TP
.BR ownership " \fB\-\-original\fR " \fIFILE\fR " \fB\-\-current\fR " \fIFILE\fR
Claim\-to\-own survival of an original paste within the current text.
.TP
.BR disclosure " \fB\-\-journal\fR " \fIFILE\fR " [\fB\-\-doc\-id\fR " \fIID\fR "]"
Render a disclosure document from a journal (a JSON array of process events).
.TP
.BR export " " \fIFILE\fR " [\fB\-\-format\fR " \fIhtml\fR|\fItext\fR "] [\fB\-\-out\fR " \fIFILE\fR "]"
Export a Markdown/Quarto document as HTML or plain text (no Quarto required).
.TP
.BR words " " \fIFILE\fR
Print word/character/line counts as JSON (\fIprose_words\fR strips Markdown
noise; \fIraw_words\fR is the unstripped tokenizer count the ownership metric
uses). The headless equivalent of the status-bar word count.
.TP
.BR open " " \fIFILE\fR
Open the editor on a file (same as passing a bare file path).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Coach configuration (overrides the saved \fB~/.config/whetstone/coach.json\fR):
.TP
.B WHETSTONE_BASE_URL
Coach endpoint, e.g. \fIhttp://localhost:11434/v1\fR (no trailing slash).
.TP
.B WHETSTONE_API_KEY
Bearer token (optional for local servers).
.TP
.B WHETSTONE_MODEL
Coach model, e.g. \fIllama3.1\fR, \fIgpt\-oss:latest\fR (default \fIgpt\-oss:latest\fR).
.TP
.B WHETSTONE_PROVIDER
\fBopenai\fR or \fBanthropic\fR (omit to auto\-detect from the URL).
.TP
.B WHETSTONE_JUDGE
\fB1\fR/\fBtrue\fR to enable the LLM judge.
.TP
.B WHETSTONE_JUDGE_MODEL
Judge model (blank inherits the coach model).
.TP
.B WHETSTONE_JUDGE_BASE_URL ", " WHETSTONE_JUDGE_API_KEY ", " WHETSTONE_JUDGE_PROVIDER
Judge endpoint overrides (blank inherits the coach's).
.PP
Preferences (override the saved \fB~/.config/whetstone/ui.json\fR):
.TP
.B WHETSTONE_THEME
Theme name, e.g. \fIFresh Dark\fR.
.TP
.B WHETSTONE_FRICTION
Friction level \fB0\fR\-\fB3\fR (Quiet / Coach / Engaged / Deep Work).
.TP
.B WHETSTONE_FRICTION_<INSTRUMENT>
Per\-instrument override (\fIPASTE\fR, \fICLAIM\fR, \fITEACHBACK\fR, \fIPUSH\fR): a level
\fB0\fR\-\fB3\fR, or \fIoff\fR/\fInone\fR/\fIpreset\fR to clear.
.TP
.B WHETSTONE_DIALECT
Grammar dialect: \fIamerican\fR, \fIbritish\fR, \fIcanadian\fR, \fIaustralian\fR, \fIindian\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/whetstone/coach.json
Coach endpoint/key/model and the optional judge. Mode \fB0600\fR on Unix.
.TP
.I ~/.config/whetstone/ui.json
Theme, friction level, per\-instrument overrides, and grammar settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/whetstone/coach\-history/
Per\-document coach chat, keyed by absolute path. Mode \fB0600\fR on Unix.
.SH KEYBINDINGS (EDITOR)
Press \fBF1\fR in the editor for the full cheat\-sheet. Notable: \fBCtrl+S\fR/\fBCtrl+O\fR
save/open, \fBCtrl+R\fR render with Quarto, \fBCtrl+Shift+E\fR/\fBCtrl+Shift+X\fR export
HTML/text, \fBCtrl+D\fR export the disclosure, \fBCtrl+E\fR AI settings, \fBCtrl+K\fR state
your claim, \fBCtrl+P\fR the process journal, \fBF10\fR the menu bar.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exits \fB0\fR on success, non\-zero on error. Headless subcommands print a JSON
document to stdout and a human\-readable error to stderr.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quarto (1)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at \fIhttps://github.com/sjvrensburg/whetstone/issues\fR. For guard
bypasses, see \fBSECURITY.md\fR (report privately rather than opening a public
issue).
